{
  "$comment": "The one definition of what counts as a DECLARED AI assistant in a commit message. Every runtime that reads commit messages for REWORK Proof loads this file and nothing else, so a commit reads the same from the Action, the App and the MCP server. Each `tools[].pattern` is a regular expression fragment written in the subset that JavaScript and Python evaluate identically: no lookbehind, no named groups, no flags inline. Matching is always case-insensitive. `patterns` are tried in order and the first hit is the verdict; `{{tools}}` expands to the alternation of every tool pattern. A match means the author DECLARED the tool in the message. No match means nothing was declared; it never means nothing was used. Version 2 (2026-11-23) adds more tools and the trailers that projects' own AI policies ask for (`Assisted-by:`, `Generated-by:`, `AI-assisted: true`). Each tool added then carries the `source` its trailer was read from; `observed` means the exact text was read there, `assumed` means it was seen only in passing or is inferred. A tool whose name is an ordinary word or a first name is matched on its address or bot login only, never on the name.",
